src/oscal/schema/*.yaml, src/oscal/datamodel/ and project/ model what the
Open Security Controls Assessment Language (OSCAL) of the National
Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST) defines. They are this
project's rendering of OSCAL 1.2.3 as a LinkML schema, with NIST as the
source of the definitions; they are not NIST's, and their use does not
imply endorsement by NIST.

OSCAL metaschema, by NIST
-------------------------

src/oscal/schema/metaschema/ holds a copy of OSCAL's metaschema sources,
retrieved from
https://github.com/usnistgov/OSCAL/tree/e061961c7702afeabffdf5e59894d35e748dade1/src/metaschema
(the v1.2.3 release), beside NIST's LICENSE.md from the root of the same
commit. Every file is identical to its counterpart there, and
scripts/check_upstream_release.py checks that it stays so. NIST's work is
in the public domain within the United States, and NIST dedicates it to the
worldwide public domain under CC0 1.0. NIST asks that a derived work
acknowledge NIST as the source and note the date and nature of its
changes; CHANGELOG.md records each release of this rendering and what it
changed.

